.TH "YAMLR-RESTORE" "1" "November 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBRestore Manifests via Atomic WAL Remediation Journal\fR
.PP
The \fByamlr restore\fR command (canonical alias for \fByamlr rollback\fR) restores Kubernetes manifests to their exact pre-remediation state using the Write-Ahead Log (WAL) forensic journal.
.PP
Whenever \fByamlr heal --apply\fR modifies files on disk, Yamlr captures an atomic pre-mutation snapshot and logs a transaction record in the remediation journal (\fB.yamlr/journal.jsonl\fR). \fByamlr restore\fR lets you list past transactions and roll back any change deterministically.
.PP
.SH "USAGE"
.nf
.RS
# List all recorded remediation transactions
yamlr restore --list

# Roll back a specific transaction by its ID
yamlr restore <TRANSACTION_ID>

# Specify a custom journal file path
yamlr restore --journal /path/to/journal.jsonl --list
.RE
.fi
.SH "OPTIONS & FLAGS"
.SS "Positional Arguments"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB[TRANSACTION]\fR: The unique transaction ID (UUID) to roll back. If omitted and \fB--list\fR is not specified, Yamlr lists recent transactions and provides rollback guidance.
.SS "Journal Controls"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB-l, --list\fR: List recent remediation transactions recorded in the journal.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB-j, --journal <PATH>\fR: Custom path to the remediation journal file. Defaults to \fB.yamlr/journal.jsonl\fR.
.SH "HOW IT WORKS"
1. \fBTransactional WAL Journal\fR: Before modifying any manifest on disk, Yamlr writes a journal record containing the file path, timestamp, and pre-remediation byte contents.
.PP
2. \fBDeterministic Reversion\fR: Passing \fB<TRANSACTION_ID>\fR reads the journal entry and atomically restores the original file content with bit-for-bit fidelity, preserving original timestamps and permissions.
.PP
3. \fBAudit Trail\fR: Rolled-back transactions are marked as \fBROLLED_BACK\fR in the journal for forensic compliance tracking.
.PP
.SH "EXIT CODES"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB0\fR (\fBEXIT_SUCCESS\fR): Transaction listed or manifest successfully restored.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB2\fR (\fBEXIT_USAGE\fR): Invalid arguments passed.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB3\fR (\fBEXIT_CONFIG_ERROR\fR): Specified transaction ID not found in journal.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB124\fR (\fBEXIT_SYSTEM_ERROR\fR): Journal unreadable or filesystem write error.
